WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.920
<i>Grew up in the military.
worked in the military.</i>

2
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.800
<i>Always told where to go. when to be there.</i>

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.420
<i>Now I see my country on my own terms.</i>

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.550
<i>Motels. cash. fake names.
Travel light.</i>

5
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.140
<i>Mostly I take buses or hitchhike.
You get used to it.</i>

6
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>Commanded the 110th</i>

7
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.520
<i>Special Investigations Unit
of the Military Police.</i>

8
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.140
You refer to these special investigators

9
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.600
<i>as your team?</i>

10
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.980
<i>They're soldiers. You need new friends.</i>

11
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.770
<i>But you know we're more than that. right?</i>

12
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.000
<i>Hundred thousand years ago
there were people</i>

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.670
<i>who stayed by the campfire.
and people who wandered.</i>

14
00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.630
<i>I'm pretty sure I'm a direct descendant
of the wandering type.</i>

15
00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.590
<i>It's just who I am.</i>

16
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:19.120
<i>♪ It was long ago ♪</i>

17
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:23.160
<i>♪ Seems like yesterday ♪</i>

18
00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:27.170
<i>♪ Saw you standing in the rain ♪</i>

19
00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:31.380
<i>♪ Then I heard you say ♪</i>

20
00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.050
<i>♪ I want to love. but it comes out wrong ♪</i>

21
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:38.220
<i>♪ I want to live but I don't belong...</i>

22
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.350
I don't care about process. just product.

23
00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.180
And this product emotes feelings.

24
00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:46.680
Hey. man. greatest song
on the subject of water.

25
00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.560
Ocean. river. stream. it doesn't matter.

26
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.770
It's gotta be "Surfin' Safari." right? So?

27
00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.730
"Surfin' Safari's" a rip-off
of Chuck Berry's "Sweet Little Sixteen."

28
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.280
so that knocks it out on principle.

29
00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.780
Oh. man.

30
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.200
Solid answer.
What can I do for you?

31
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.620
Your sign says you buy vinyl.

32
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:05.250
<i>♪ Her blood ran cold
and then she said...</i>

33
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.370
<i>Ethel Merman Disco Album.</i>

34
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.170
- Are you shitting me?
- But this is a college town.

35
00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.670
Some hipster will buy 'em to be ironic.

36
00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.920
No...

37
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.470
<i>♪ I close my eyes and I see ♪</i>

38
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.590
<i>♪ Blood and roses ♪</i>

39
00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.000
What the hell?

40
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.380
Oh. Oh. no! No. no. no. no. no!

41
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.930
Okay.

42
00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.060
Okay...

43
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.170
- No. Please?
- I'm not gonna hurt you.

44
00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.920
- Get in.
- Well. I--

45
00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.050
They may have backup on the way.

46
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.890
Hey!

47
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.980
You shot a cop.

48
00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.610
I didn't know.

49
00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.860
I thought he was pulling a gun.

50
00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:59.860
- We got to go. Now!
- What?

51
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.000
Why are people trying to kidnap you?

52
00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.050
Campus police?

53
00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.090
- Are you shitting me?
- Pull over.

54
00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:24.590
I killed a cop with an illegal gun!

55
00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:25.760
Well. it was an accident.

56
00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.050
I'm not explaining my way out of this.

57
00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.680
Get down!

58
00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.810
Look out!

59
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.960
Hang on.

60
00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.040
Oh!

61
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.390
You could have killed 'em!

62
00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.270
I slowed 'em enough to limit the impact.

63
00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.140
But I bet they called the real cops.

64
00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.730
I got to find a new ride.

65
00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.290
Uh...

66
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.460
We're only a few miles from campus.

67
00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.090
There could be more kidnappers
coming up right behind us.

68
00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.500
You're gonna steal it?

69
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.210
Parked out back with a sun shade?

70
00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.840
Probably belongs to an employee
who won't notice it's missing

71
00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:50.340
till tonight.

72
00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.890
Gives me a head start.

73
00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.480
Keep an eye out.

74
00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:58.730
Aah. Hey. where'd you learn
to do all this stuff?

75
00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.190
Steal cars. drive like that?

76
00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.570
- Shoot people?
- Army.

77
00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:05.490
Other stuff I picked up here and there.

78
00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.450
You got a phone?

79
00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.990
Uh. why?

80
00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.370
So you can call for a ride.

81
00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.500
Tell 'em you're in shock
and can't remember what I look like.

82
00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.790
What? No!
You can't just leave me here.

83
00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.960
What if those guys find me?

84
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.210
What am I supposed to do?
Take you to the cops?

85
00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:24.960
I can't do that after what I did.

86
00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.260
So then take me home.

87
00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.920
No.

88
00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.470
Done enough for you for one day.

89
00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.970
I got to disappear.

90
00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:36.350
Please.

91
00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.810
I'm a drifter who used an unlicensed gun
to kill a cop.

92
00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.110
I'm not taking any chances.

93
00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.860
I'm getting lost.

94
00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.360
My dad's rich.

95
00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.530
And connected.
He can... he can help you.

96
00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:49.280
Why would he do that?

97
00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.370
Well. you saved his son.

98
00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.950
That cop was an accident. Right?

99
00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.290
So. look. he'll j...
he'll just be grateful

100
00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.830
that you kept me
from getting kidnapped again.

101
00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:02.170
- Again?
- First time was five years ago.

102
00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.540
That what happened to your ear?

103
00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.000
They wanted to make a point.

104
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.710
- 'Cause your dad wouldn't pay the ransom?
- Yeah.

105
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.010
After he got my ear in the mail. he paid.

106
00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.970
Not as bad as you did.

107
00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:18.600
Kidnapping is a rare crime
in this country.

108
00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.730
Pretty unlucky
it almost happened to you twice.

109
00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.230
What does your father do for a living?

110
00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.440
Imports rugs.

111
00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.730
That all he imports?

112
00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.900
He's just a rug merchant.

113
00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.900
But he's got generational wealth.
and that makes me a target.

114
00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.280
So the guy who got blown up
in your car wasn't your driver.

115
00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.580
- He was your bodyguard.
- Yeah.

116
00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.000
Tell your dad
to hire a better one next time.

117
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.080
Guy who took a run at you was a pro.

118
00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.710
If it hadn't been for me.
it would have worked.

119
00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.580
Okay. so then. take me home

120
00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.340
and let my dad repay you for what you did.

121
00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:49.090
Y-You want to disappear?
You-you need money? He has money.

122
00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.420
Please.

123
00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:57.560
You got a name. kid?

124
00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.600
Richard. Richard Beck.

125
00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.400
Get in. Richard.

126
00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.940
- Get out of the car.
-  Yeah. it's all right. Paulie.

127
00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.480
I talked to my dad
and told him we were coming.

128
00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:52.190
I don't give a shit.

129
00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.700
Get out.

130
00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.070
No.

131
00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.700
Just let him do it.

132
00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:02.040
- He's rude.
- Please.

133
00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.850
You know what I'm hoping to find?

134
00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.730
More HGH and a hypodermic needle?

135
00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:33.900
A reason to kick your ass. shithead.

136
00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:37.200
And maybe you just gave it to me.

137
00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.490
Uh...

138
00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:44.120
His-his gun is in the glove compartment.
Paulie.

139
00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.290
Here. just take it.

140
00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.130
Why is it empty?

141
00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:52.090
Because I shot all the bullets.

142
00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.480
Lot of security for a rug merchant.

143
00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.900
I told you. He's rich.

144
00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:20.870
<i>Your dad's employees always</i>

145
00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.990
talk like that to his son's friends?

146
00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:28.210
Paul Van Hoven does whatever he wants.

147
00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:39.380
Yeah. Oh. are... are you hungry?

148
00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:41.590
Sure.

149
00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.100
I'll make him a plate.

150
00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:45.640
I can just take that one on the counter.

151
00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:49.190
That's not for you.
And you don't have time to eat.

152
00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.440
Beck wants to see you.

153
00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:53.060
Office is upstairs.
down the hall and to the right.

154
00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.570
Uh. I can show you.

155
00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.900
No. He wants to see him alone.

156
00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.530
And that's Chapman Duke. head of security.

157
00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:06.200
Why is he eating outside?

158
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:09.410
Who knows? But you better do what he says.

159
00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.640
Mr. Reacher.

160
00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.350
Just... Reacher.

161
00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.850
Noted.

162
00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.770
I'm Zachary Beck.

163
00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:35.520
You had some morning.

164
00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:38.070
I bet you could use a drink.

165
00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.740
This is 50-year-old Macallan.

166
00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.360
I only open it
for my top business associates...

167
00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.660
and people who save my son's life.

168
00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.500
Suit yourself.

169
00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:00.420
Have a seat there.

170
00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.140
Okay. fine.

171
00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:10.980
Don't sit.

172
00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.980
I'm sure you heard what Richard told me
about the attempted kidnapping

173
00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.730
when he called me from the car.

174
00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.230
What can you add to that?

175
00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:19.530
Just that the guy you hired
to look after him was useless.

176
00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.820
- You're speaking ill of the dead.
- A ratty old pickup

177
00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.110
hanging around a rich-kid college town?

178
00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.450
What kind of bodyguard doesn't clock that?

179
00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:28.530
But you noticed a detail that small.

180
00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.700
I tend to do that.

181
00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.910
What makes you so good
at threat assessment?

182
00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.620
I was in the Army. MP.

183
00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.750
I was trying to unload records

184
00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.340
- for some extra cash.
- Is that your job?

185
00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.090
Selling used records
in New England college towns?

186
00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:47.260
There a lot of money in that?

187
00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.350
- Don't have a job.
- So. how do you pay the rent?

188
00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:51.270
Don't have a home.

189
00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.060
- I move around a lot.
- With a gun?

190
00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.690
Wherever I go.
trouble just seems to find me.

191
00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:59.980
I understand you accidentally
killed a police officer.

192
00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.780
I just need a place
to lie low for a few days

193
00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.240
and then some money to buy
a fake I.D. for a clean start.

194
00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.700
That's no small ask.

195
00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:09.530
But I do owe you.

196
00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:14.080
Let me think it over and I'll...

197
00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.920
figure out the best way I can be of help.

198
00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.330
Okay.

199
00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.710
Duke.

200
00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.460
Sir. could you show Mr. Reacher
back to the kitchen. please?

201
00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:26.220
I believe Agnes has
some nice shepherd's pie.

202
00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:41.110
I gripped it firmly so you'll have
a clear set of prints to run.

203
00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:46.240
Don't be offended. Mr. Reacher.

204
00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.780
Just need to know who you are.

205
00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:53.290
I'm the guy who saved
your son's other ear.

206
00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:08.220
If I go in to hit the head.
you gonna hold it for me?

207
00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.760
If I want to.

208
00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.180
Hey. hey. where are you going?

209
00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.600
- To check on the kid.
- We'll take care of him.

210
00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.650
Like your guy did this morning?

211
00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.800
You forgot to add the guard house.

212
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:49.130
No. I didn't.

213
00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.550
How was your talk with my dad?

214
00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:56.270
He has trust issues.

215
00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:59.190
Surprised he hasn't come to check on you.
Considering all that happened.

216
00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.560
We talked on the phone. He knows I'm okay.

217
00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:08.150
He'll check on me soon.

218
00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:11.870
Okay.

219
00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:18.290
Where's your mother?

220
00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.750
Since I was four.
St. Sebastian's Cemetery.

221
00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:36.810
You only paint what you see
out those windows?

222
00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.600
Paint what you know.

223
00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.060
You ever paint. Reacher?

224
00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.480
No.

225
00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:48.570
Well. if you did. what would it be of?

226
00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.360
I don't know.

227
00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:54.070
Dogs. maybe.

228
00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.370
Beck wants to see you.

229
00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.540
Guess it's back to the office.

230
00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:04.250
We're not going back to the office.

231
00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:18.680
Sit.

232
00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.480
Today's excitement made the news.

233
00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.610
Lot of buzz for a college town.

234
00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:28.440
I get made?

235
00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:30.980
Guys at the record shop
gave a general description.

236
00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:35.120
but that could match
any inside linebacker. so...

237
00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.030
...no one knows who you are.

238
00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.290
But we do.

239
00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.160
We ran your prints.

240
00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.670
That was fast.

241
00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:48.250
Must have some serious connections.

242
00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.670
Everything we do here is serious.

243
00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:56.090
Your record is impressive.

244
00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:57.720
West Point graduate.

245
00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.140
Two Silver Stars.

246
00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:00.640
Purple Heart.

247
00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:02.060
Green clovers. blue diamonds.

248
00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:04.890
He's a fucking bowl of Lucky Charms.

249
00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:06.400
Paulie was in the Army. too.

250
00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.480
He doesn't like officers.

251
00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:12.860
You failed the OCS exam.

252
00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.360
Not surprised.

253
00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.320
You don't look like you could spell OCS.

254
00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:19.660
What if I could do more
than give you a couple bucks. Reacher?

255
00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.160
At a time we're short a man.
it appears we're under attack.

256
00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:24.750
'Cause you're a rug merchant?

257
00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.750
Because I'm wealthy. And powerful.

258
00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.840
So I hear.

259
00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.710
And because of that. you want to hire me?

260
00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.010
Maybe.

261
00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:38.050
But first a little test.

262
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.020
What am I supposed to do with that?

263
00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:47.100
You're gonna play
Russian roulette. asshole.

264
00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:52.020
Federal law prevents you from asking me
if I'm married during a job interview.

265
00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:53.530
so I'm pretty sure this isn't allowed.

266
00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.900
I need to see if you have any stones.

267
00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.410
If you can follow orders.

268
00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:02.410
- To work for a rug merchant.
- You shot a cop.

269
00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:04.410
We can turn you in
or you can do what you're told.

270
00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.040
Those are your choices.

271
00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.600
What if I just shoot you instead?

272
00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.730
That would be the last thing you do.

273
00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.790
Good. We got that out of the way.

274
00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:04.310
You proved your point.

275
00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:13.270
Welcome to the team. Reacher.
Duke will get you squared away.

276
00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.450
You're kidding.

277
00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:26.080
Thought I was on the team.

278
00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.870
I got enough crazy
on my hands with Paulie.

279
00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:30.250
I don't need your big ass
walking around here with a gun. too.

280
00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.500
I'm not crazy.

281
00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:34.540
I know the bullet didn't have
any powder in it. It's a dud.

282
00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.760
What would you have done
if I had killed myself?

283
00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:47.930
Same thing we did with the last guy.

284
00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.660
Let's go!

285
00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.640
You start first thing in the morning.
You're locked in until then.

286
00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.800
Why?

287
00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:28.600
Because Beck might trust you now.
but I don't.

288
00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:31.060
- What if I don't like that arrangement?
- Call the cops.

289
00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:09.510
-  <i>Yeah?</i>
- I'm in.

290
00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:44.840
Wait.

291
00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.300
Wait! Wait!

292
00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.510
Wait!

293
00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:57.190
Hey. We'll catch the next one. okay?

294
00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:13.490
Don't do it.

295
00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:14.790
What?

296
00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:19.130
You're gonna take the next bus
with that woman and steal from her bag.

297
00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:22.090
Fuck you.

298
00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:24.880
Only one bus runs on this line.

299
00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:27.420
You didn't take the last one
'cause your marks were bad.

300
00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:30.090
One guy had a locked briefcase.
the other two didn't have anything.

301
00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:33.220
The woman at the end of this bench

302
00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:37.270
has an unclasped purse and a four-year-old
taking up most of her attention.

303
00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:39.810
Easy pickings.

304
00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:41.440
Are you a cop?

305
00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:44.110
Don't need to be
to see your clumsy approach.

306
00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:46.190
Exact fare in quarters?

307
00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:50.530
What teenager after 1994 walks around
with quarters in their pocket?

308
00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:52.370
No.

309
00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.370
You're new at this.

310
00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:56.450
If you were a pro. you'd have a bus pass.

311
00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:00.250
What are you gonna do?

312
00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:07.670
Here.

313
00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:10.430
You need money. right? Take it.

314
00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:12.890
Then go get a job.

315
00:23:12.890 --> 00:23:15.760
Because the next guy who catches you
stealing might not give you a hundred.

316
00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:17.680
He might give you a beating.

317
00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:20.020
Thanks.

318
00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:41.500
Give me your phone.

319
00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:47.340
110th Special Investigators.
Warrant Officer Powell speaking.

320
00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:50.170
This is Jack Reacher.
I need to speak to your C.O. immediately.

321
00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:52.550
Sorry. sir. Major Turner is unavailable.

322
00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:54.550
Tell her to call me back ASAP.

323
00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:56.050
<i>I'm calling in that favor she owes me.</i>

324
00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:59.020
I can do that. sir.
but she won't get the note for a while.

325
00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:00.640
She's on assignment.

326
00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:03.940
Undercover and incommunicado
for at least two weeks.

327
00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:05.650
Is this really Major Reacher?

328
00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:08.190
Like. the Jack Reacher
who started the 110th?

329
00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:10.030
It is.

330
00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:11.780
I need your help. Powell.

331
00:24:11.780 --> 00:24:13.450
<i>Whatever you need. sir.</i>

332
00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:16.830
- Run a license plate for me.
- <i>Of course. Shoot.</i>

333
00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:17.990
Civilian. Maine.

334
00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:19.750
Seven. Seven. Four. Oh. Tango. Lima.

335
00:24:20.910 --> 00:24:22.330
Running now.

336
00:24:23.540 --> 00:24:25.250
Hey. uh...

337
00:24:25.250 --> 00:24:26.920
mind if I ask you a question?

338
00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:29.550
Shoot.

339
00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:33.510
Your old desk is still here
and there's a dent

340
00:24:33.510 --> 00:24:34.840
on the right-hand side.

341
00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:37.350
Legend is you made it
with a colonel's head.

342
00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:38.560
That true?

343
00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.730
David O'Donnell did that messing around
with Stan Lowrey's bowling ball.

344
00:24:41.730 --> 00:24:43.230
<i>Lowrey got back at him by drawing</i>

345
00:24:43.230 --> 00:24:45.770
genitals on his face
when O'Donnell fell asleep on the couch.

346
00:24:45.770 --> 00:24:49.230
Man. we've heard stories
about those guys. too.

347
00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:51.690
Looks like something's up
with their system.

348
00:24:51.690 --> 00:24:54.530
I can give you a call when I get it.
Can I reach you at this number?

349
00:24:54.530 --> 00:24:58.120
No. Take down where I'm staying.

350
00:25:06.750 --> 00:25:09.000
Federal agents. Open up.

351
00:25:53.170 --> 00:25:54.710
Where you going. Mr. Reacher?

352
00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:56.340
Who says my name's Reacher?

353
00:25:56.340 --> 00:25:57.970
Not the guy that runs this shithole.

354
00:25:57.970 --> 00:26:00.390
He says you registered as Rob Refsnyder.

355
00:26:00.390 --> 00:26:02.760
but you don't look much
like a middle infielder to me.

356
00:26:02.770 --> 00:26:05.140
Now. do you wanna talk by the dumpster

357
00:26:05.140 --> 00:26:08.900
or can we find a place
that smells less like vomit?

358
00:26:15.070 --> 00:26:17.030
Nice place.

359
00:26:17.030 --> 00:26:19.070
- Motel 6 was booked.
- Mm.

360
00:26:19.070 --> 00:26:21.740
This is like a Motel 2.

361
00:26:21.740 --> 00:26:24.080
It's not like I invited you here.
Agent...?

362
00:26:24.080 --> 00:26:26.910
Duffy. Susan Duffy.
The two you left standing at the door

363
00:26:26.910 --> 00:26:29.960
with their dicks in their hands
are Eliot and Villanueva.

364
00:26:29.960 --> 00:26:31.710
Why'd you run?

365
00:26:31.710 --> 00:26:34.090
We identified ourselves as federal agents.

366
00:26:34.090 --> 00:26:35.670
Anyone can say they're anything.

367
00:26:35.670 --> 00:26:39.550
This place attracts a criminal element.
I panicked.

368
00:26:39.550 --> 00:26:42.850
You don't seem like
the panicking type. Mr. Reacher.

369
00:26:44.060 --> 00:26:45.560
Just Reacher.

370
00:26:45.560 --> 00:26:48.060
Okay. Reacher. Why do you use an alias?

371
00:26:48.060 --> 00:26:49.440
I like my privacy.

372
00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:52.020
- Is that why you gave no address?
- No.

373
00:26:52.020 --> 00:26:54.190
Then why no address?

374
00:26:54.190 --> 00:26:55.570
Because I don't have one.

375
00:26:55.570 --> 00:26:57.190
What are you doing in Maine?

376
00:26:57.190 --> 00:26:58.570
I wanted good lobster.

377
00:26:58.570 --> 00:27:01.610
- We're being serious.
- So am I.

378
00:27:01.620 --> 00:27:05.290
I was in Cape May. I had subpar lobster.
wanted better. so I came up here.

379
00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:08.830
- You think this is funny?
- I think this is a waste of my time.

380
00:27:08.830 --> 00:27:12.540
I don't know what you want from me.
but I know I want nothing from you.

381
00:27:12.540 --> 00:27:14.790
So I'm going back to my room.

382
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:18.590
To wait for a call
from Warrant Officer Powell?

383
00:27:19.930 --> 00:27:21.630
Don't bother. It's not coming.

384
00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:24.760
So. why don't you drop
your seat warmer in that chair.

385
00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:27.930
You can finish feeding Daffy
and we can finish our conversation.

386
00:27:29.390 --> 00:27:31.190
Powell gave you up.

387
00:27:31.190 --> 00:27:35.320
He wouldn't roll till we threatened him
with obstructing a federal investigation.

388
00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:38.740
- Kid was nearly in tears.
- Fuckin' embarrassing.

389
00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:40.240
What federal investigation?

390
00:27:40.240 --> 00:27:43.910
We're looking into a rug import business
called Bizarre Bazaar.

391
00:27:43.910 --> 00:27:46.490
And the DEA think rugs
aren't the only thing they're importing.

392
00:27:46.490 --> 00:27:49.700
Several weeks ago.
a high-level. L.A.-based drug dealer

393
00:27:49.710 --> 00:27:52.580
flew to Maine for a meeting
with the owner of Bizarre Bazaar.

394
00:27:52.580 --> 00:27:55.840
Major drug runners don't travel
3.000 miles to buy carpets.

395
00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:58.250
So we figure the owner
of Bizarre Bazaar is his supplier.

396
00:27:58.260 --> 00:28:01.050
Which would make him
responsible for most of the poison

397
00:28:01.050 --> 00:28:03.800
being pumped into
the Western United States.

398
00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:05.680
Problem is. we can't
dig anything up on the guy.

399
00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:07.220
Not even an address.

400
00:28:07.220 --> 00:28:10.390
Figure the property's set up
under an LLC or something.

401
00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:12.980
What's this got to do with me?

402
00:28:12.980 --> 00:28:15.610
The license plate you ran
was screwed to the car

403
00:28:15.610 --> 00:28:17.980
that brought the Carpet King
to that meeting.

404
00:28:17.980 --> 00:28:20.820
We flagged the number on the system
so Powell tripped our alarm

405
00:28:20.820 --> 00:28:22.490
when he looked it up for you.

406
00:28:22.490 --> 00:28:23.780
Why were you checking the plate?

407
00:28:23.780 --> 00:28:25.740
Maybe the driver hit my car and ran off.

408
00:28:25.740 --> 00:28:27.620
Did he hit your car and run off?

409
00:28:27.620 --> 00:28:29.040
I don't own a car.

410
00:28:35.790 --> 00:28:37.090
Zachary Beck. You know him?

411
00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:40.420
Shit's sake. Eliot. you don't
give the guy we're questioning

412
00:28:40.420 --> 00:28:43.590
the name of the subject.
then ask if he knows him.

413
00:28:43.590 --> 00:28:45.550
Sorry. Shit.

414
00:28:45.550 --> 00:28:47.560
I don't know him.

415
00:28:49.680 --> 00:28:51.890
You recognize anyone here?

416
00:28:51.890 --> 00:28:53.060
No.

417
00:28:54.190 --> 00:28:56.650
I'll tell you what I think.
I think you saw someone in that car

418
00:28:56.650 --> 00:28:59.070
you did recognize
and now you're looking for them.

419
00:28:59.070 --> 00:29:00.230
So who was it?

420
00:29:01.900 --> 00:29:04.610
According to Powell.
you were some kind of Army super-cop.

421
00:29:04.610 --> 00:29:06.990
We checked you out.
More awards than Tom Brady.

422
00:29:06.990 --> 00:29:08.120
Fuck that traitor.

423
00:29:08.120 --> 00:29:10.580
That's why we're coming to you now.
We need your help.

424
00:29:12.080 --> 00:29:14.710
Then you really must be desperate.

425
00:29:14.710 --> 00:29:17.170
- Buddy. you don't know the half of it.
-  And I don't want to.

426
00:29:17.170 --> 00:29:19.250
At least until you do something for me.

427
00:29:20.960 --> 00:29:23.340
You're not the kind of guy
I wanna do a favor for.

428
00:29:23.340 --> 00:29:25.590
- Why is that?
- You're a pain in the ass.

429
00:29:25.590 --> 00:29:27.180
You answer questions like an asshole.

430
00:29:27.180 --> 00:29:29.810
- You always so direct?
- You always so frustrating?

431
00:29:34.640 --> 00:29:36.730
So what can I do for you. Reacher?

432
00:29:36.730 --> 00:29:38.980
Check hospital records
around Linton. Virginia

433
00:29:38.980 --> 00:29:41.270
on or just after March 13th. 2012.

434
00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.860
- What are we looking for?
- An Asian American man in his 40s.

435
00:29:43.860 --> 00:29:45.280
brought in with injuries consistent

436
00:29:45.280 --> 00:29:47.160
with a small-caliber gunshot wound
to the head.

437
00:29:47.160 --> 00:29:49.620
a high fall and drowning.
Look. you're the Feds.

438
00:29:49.620 --> 00:29:52.330
You've got resources.
You find something. call me.

439
00:29:52.330 --> 00:29:54.960
Maybe then we can talk about
what you need.

440
00:30:16.190 --> 00:30:18.100
So. we found your guy.

441
00:30:18.100 --> 00:30:22.820
Washed up on a beach barely alive
just south of. uh. whatsit. Virginia.

442
00:30:22.820 --> 00:30:25.070
- Linton.
- Whatever.

443
00:30:25.070 --> 00:30:26.900
Wounds matched your description.

444
00:30:26.900 --> 00:30:30.530
Small-caliber bullet lodged in his skull.
massive internal injuries.

445
00:30:30.530 --> 00:30:32.330
Some beachcomber found him.

446
00:30:32.330 --> 00:30:34.700
Doctors figure
the freezin' water saved him.

447
00:30:34.700 --> 00:30:36.790
- Hypothermia.
- Yup.

448
00:30:36.790 --> 00:30:38.210
Slowed his heart so he didn't bleed.

449
00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:40.630
decreased oxygen demand
prevented brain damage.

450
00:30:40.630 --> 00:30:43.880
Took the docs about six months
to put Humpty Dumpty together again.

451
00:30:43.880 --> 00:30:46.260
He tell the medical staff
what happened to him?

452
00:30:46.260 --> 00:30:47.880
Claimed he didn't remember.

453
00:30:47.880 --> 00:30:48.930
File?

454
00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:52.050
Psychiatrists
interviewed the guy regularly

455
00:30:52.050 --> 00:30:53.260
when he was in the hospital.

456
00:30:53.260 --> 00:30:55.640
He stuck to his story.

457
00:30:55.640 --> 00:30:57.600
Do you see anyone else eating?

458
00:30:57.600 --> 00:30:59.770
What? I was at the Kinko's
first thing copying the files.

459
00:30:59.770 --> 00:31:02.270
- I didn't have time for break--
- They diagnosed traumatic amnesia.

460
00:31:02.270 --> 00:31:04.900
Thought he was probably
genuinely blank about the incident

461
00:31:04.900 --> 00:31:06.690
and the previous day or two.

462
00:31:06.690 --> 00:31:09.150
but they figured he must
remember things from before that.

463
00:31:09.150 --> 00:31:12.530
They got the impression
maybe he was pretending not to.

464
00:31:12.530 --> 00:31:14.910
They kept questioning him.
but he never cracked.

465
00:31:14.910 --> 00:31:16.950
Local cops look into it?

466
00:31:16.950 --> 00:31:19.660
County sheriff ran his prints.
but they weren't in the system.

467
00:31:19.670 --> 00:31:23.130
He also didn't match any missing persons
and no one came looking for him.

468
00:31:23.130 --> 00:31:24.630
so he stayed a John Doe.

469
00:31:24.630 --> 00:31:26.500
But from the way you're eye-fucking him.

470
00:31:26.510 --> 00:31:28.130
I think you know his name.

471
00:31:31.640 --> 00:31:34.850
Fuck you. big boy.
I showed you mine. you show me yours.

472
00:31:34.850 --> 00:31:36.470
Or are there no rules where you come from?

473
00:31:36.470 --> 00:31:38.100
I don't really come from anywhere.

474
00:31:38.100 --> 00:31:40.060
Well. I did. And on Emerson Street.

475
00:31:40.060 --> 00:31:42.810
if you didn't do what's right.
you got your ears boxed.

476
00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:52.410
Lieutenant Colonel Francis Xavier Quinn.

477
00:31:52.410 --> 00:31:54.240
Military Intelligence.

478
00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:57.290
Picked up extra cash selling
military secrets to hostile nations.

479
00:31:58.620 --> 00:32:00.200
We were never able to execute an arrest.

480
00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:03.370
- Who threw him off a cliff?
- Maybe an unsatisfied customer.

481
00:32:03.380 --> 00:32:05.040
He was in business with bad people.

482
00:32:06.050 --> 00:32:08.630
If this guy was Army. his fingerprints
should've been in the system.

483
00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:11.300
He had deep connections through M.I.

484
00:32:11.300 --> 00:32:14.050
Figure someone on the inside wiped 'em
from his file when he went on the run.

485
00:32:14.050 --> 00:32:15.850
Photos too. maybe.

486
00:32:16.850 --> 00:32:19.060
You saw Quinn in Beck's car.

487
00:32:19.060 --> 00:32:20.560
Yeah.

488
00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:22.520
And now you wanna find him.

489
00:32:23.940 --> 00:32:25.520
Yeah.

490
00:32:25.520 --> 00:32:27.270
So maybe we can
help each other out.

491
00:32:27.270 --> 00:32:29.070
Let's take a walk.

492
00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:37.200
Look. I think I can trust you.

493
00:32:37.200 --> 00:32:39.620
but I'm trying to figure out for sure.

494
00:32:40.790 --> 00:32:42.250
Why?

495
00:32:42.250 --> 00:32:44.370
Because I screwed up.

496
00:32:44.380 --> 00:32:48.290
Weeks of surveillance on Darien Prado.
he's the L.A. drug dealer.

497
00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:51.260
all inadmissible because of a bad warrant.

498
00:32:51.260 --> 00:32:53.260
How'd that happen?

499
00:32:53.260 --> 00:32:56.550
We surveilled and filmed him
from what we thought was public land--

500
00:32:56.550 --> 00:32:59.140
national forest. middle of nowhere--

501
00:32:59.140 --> 00:33:02.350
but it abutted private property.

502
00:33:02.350 --> 00:33:04.980
We were 20 feet over the line
and didn't know it.

503
00:33:04.980 --> 00:33:07.860
Warrant didn't let us film from there.

504
00:33:07.860 --> 00:33:09.820
You misread the surveyor's map?

505
00:33:09.820 --> 00:33:12.360
It was a real shit show. okay?

506
00:33:12.360 --> 00:33:16.360
Ton of work down the crapper
and the DEA pulled us off the case.

507
00:33:16.370 --> 00:33:18.200
Now you're working it off the books?

508
00:33:18.200 --> 00:33:21.290
I don't let bad guys walk.

509
00:33:21.290 --> 00:33:23.710
And I'm a team leader.
No one's watchin' my day-to-day.

510
00:33:23.710 --> 00:33:26.870
So now you're focused on Beck?

511
00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:30.210
Prado flew all the way out here
to meet with him.

512
00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:32.380
so Beck could be a bigger fish.

513
00:33:32.380 --> 00:33:35.510
And if we net him.
we get Prado too. right?

514
00:33:35.510 --> 00:33:38.930
But Beck turned out to be a ghost.
Can't find out shit on him.

515
00:33:38.930 --> 00:33:42.310
So I got the bright idea
to reach out to an old C.I.

516
00:33:42.310 --> 00:33:45.230
Something tells me that didn't
work out like you planned.

517
00:33:45.230 --> 00:33:47.980
It's this kid named Teresa Daniel.

518
00:33:47.980 --> 00:33:50.730
Few years ago. she was tricked
by her scumbag boyfriend

519
00:33:50.730 --> 00:33:53.070
into delivering car parts
stuffed with coke.

520
00:33:53.070 --> 00:33:54.570
She had no idea.

521
00:33:54.570 --> 00:33:58.530
I busted her. flipped her. turned out
to be the best C.I. I ever had.

522
00:33:58.530 --> 00:34:02.030
This kid is so innocent. so unassuming...

523
00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:05.710
- No one suspects she's a plant.
- No one. She's a natural C.I.

524
00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:09.460
So when I saw Bizarre Bazaar had
a help wanted ad online for a secretary.

525
00:34:09.460 --> 00:34:10.960
I called Teresa.

526
00:34:10.960 --> 00:34:13.340
She lives with her grandmother.
she takes care of her.

527
00:34:13.340 --> 00:34:15.760
so I knew she needed money.

528
00:34:15.760 --> 00:34:18.010
She got the job
at Bizarre Bazaar's warehouse

529
00:34:18.010 --> 00:34:21.510
and was gonna just report back
what Beck was up to in there.

530
00:34:21.510 --> 00:34:23.020
But?

531
00:34:25.310 --> 00:34:28.020
About a week ago. she disappeared.

532
00:34:29.310 --> 00:34:32.520
I don't hear from her.
her grandma's got no idea where she is.

533
00:34:32.520 --> 00:34:35.860
She called Bizarre Bazaar. but they
said she never showed up for work.

534
00:34:35.860 --> 00:34:39.280
so the old lady's sure
her granddaughter's using again.

535
00:34:40.370 --> 00:34:41.870
But you think there's more to it.

536
00:34:41.870 --> 00:34:44.830
I know junkies. Teresa was past all that.

537
00:34:44.830 --> 00:34:46.830
She'd turned it around.

538
00:34:46.830 --> 00:34:48.830
I think she got caught snooping on Beck

539
00:34:48.830 --> 00:34:50.880
and something happened to her.

540
00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:53.880
I gotta find out what. but no judge
is gonna issue a warrant

541
00:34:53.880 --> 00:34:56.050
to search a prominent local businessman

542
00:34:56.050 --> 00:34:58.510
over an ex-druggie blowing off work.

543
00:34:58.510 --> 00:35:01.220
Like. she's 20.
but she's still just a kid.

544
00:35:03.390 --> 00:35:06.770
Look. She wears these.
uh. giant hoop earrings

545
00:35:06.770 --> 00:35:08.640
like my niece and her friends.

546
00:35:10.690 --> 00:35:12.560
Why are you showing me this?

547
00:35:14.150 --> 00:35:15.900
'Cause you need to know
what she looks like

548
00:35:15.900 --> 00:35:19.320
when I put you inside Beck's
operation to find her.

549
00:35:19.320 --> 00:35:21.990
I hate to break it to you.
but if Teresa was taken by someone

550
00:35:21.990 --> 00:35:25.160
associated with Xavier Quinn.
odds are you're too late.

551
00:35:25.160 --> 00:35:27.160
Why would you say something
like that to me?

552
00:35:27.160 --> 00:35:28.910
Because you're too smart to lie to.

553
00:35:28.910 --> 00:35:31.040
You'd see through it.

554
00:35:31.040 --> 00:35:32.210
He's that bad?

555
00:35:32.210 --> 00:35:34.420
He's the single worst person
I've ever known.

556
00:35:34.420 --> 00:35:37.050
Well. all the more reason
for you to get on board.

557
00:35:37.050 --> 00:35:38.460
You need to find Quinn.

558
00:35:38.470 --> 00:35:41.760
While you're doing that.
you can help me find Teresa.

559
00:35:41.760 --> 00:35:45.640
You know. I'm not just a pretty face.
I have a plan.

560
00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:50.390
Zachary Beck's son. Richard.

561
00:35:50.390 --> 00:35:52.600
Five years ago. he was kidnapped.

562
00:35:52.600 --> 00:35:55.520
You know how often people
get kidnapped in America these days?

563
00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:58.480
Could be a turf war thing.
Rival drug dealers.

564
00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:01.200
Especially since the kidnappers
cut off the kid's ear

565
00:36:01.200 --> 00:36:04.370
and mailed it to Beck. who.
by the way. never went to the cops.

566
00:36:04.370 --> 00:36:06.580
How do you know about it. then?

567
00:36:06.580 --> 00:36:10.790
Well. you walk around a college campus
with a missing ear and kids ask questions.

568
00:36:10.790 --> 00:36:14.250
Richard answered some of 'em.
and one of his classmates talked

569
00:36:14.250 --> 00:36:16.590
in exchange for us
dropping some minor drug charges.

570
00:36:16.590 --> 00:36:20.340
So the Beck kid's had it rough.
What's he got to do with your plan?

571
00:36:20.340 --> 00:36:22.470
You're gonna get in with Beck

572
00:36:22.470 --> 00:36:24.970
by saving his son
from getting kidnapped again.

573
00:36:24.970 --> 00:36:28.350
- Undercover informant?
- Yeah. what's the problem?

574
00:36:28.350 --> 00:36:30.100
The last one you had went missing.

575
00:36:30.100 --> 00:36:33.980
You remember what I said earlier
about you being an asshole?

576
00:36:33.980 --> 00:36:35.940
You're doing it right now.

577
00:36:40.110 --> 00:36:43.030
All right. so we get a solid
car from the DEA impound.

578
00:36:43.030 --> 00:36:46.490
ram the hell outta the bodyguard's car.
pin it so that it can't move.

579
00:36:46.490 --> 00:36:48.080
We still gotta deal with the guy.

580
00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:49.870
And he's no pushover either.

581
00:36:49.870 --> 00:36:52.790
Got a jacket and a half:
aggravated assault. armed robbery.

582
00:36:52.790 --> 00:36:54.120
He'll know how to use his gun.

583
00:36:54.120 --> 00:36:56.040
Great. How we gonna
keep from getting shot?

584
00:36:56.040 --> 00:36:58.040
'Cause we can't just kill the man.

585
00:36:58.050 --> 00:37:00.380
Hey. here he is. Gimme.

586
00:37:01.800 --> 00:37:04.220
- What's this shit? I said Dink's.
- A doughnut's a doughnut.

587
00:37:04.220 --> 00:37:05.380
Shut your filthy mouth.

588
00:37:05.390 --> 00:37:07.090
Okay. fine. I'll eat 'em all. then.

589
00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:08.350
Didn't say I didn't want 'em.

590
00:37:08.350 --> 00:37:10.810
- You take your Lipitor today?
- Still waiting on the refill.

591
00:37:10.810 --> 00:37:13.230
Oh.

592
00:37:13.230 --> 00:37:16.020
Let's say the impact
rings the bodyguard's bell.

593
00:37:16.020 --> 00:37:18.650
Doesn't mean he won't get a few shots off.

594
00:37:18.650 --> 00:37:21.900
Duffy's right. We need more.

595
00:37:23.860 --> 00:37:25.610
In Kuwait. we'd used flashbang grenades

596
00:37:25.610 --> 00:37:28.490
when we wanted to keep
a target alive for interrogation.

597
00:37:28.490 --> 00:37:31.740
Bodyguard won't be seriously injured.
but he'll be in no condition to retaliate.

598
00:37:31.750 --> 00:37:35.710
It'll blow out the windows.
really sell the lie to Richard.

599
00:37:35.710 --> 00:37:38.710
And it'll create a job opening.
Beck will need a new bodyguard.

600
00:37:38.710 --> 00:37:40.500
Okay. sorry. I'm confused.

601
00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:42.210
- Shocking.
-  If the bodyguard
isn't really dead.

602
00:37:42.210 --> 00:37:44.550
he can just go tell Beck
what actually happened.

603
00:37:44.550 --> 00:37:46.970
So how do we get around that?

604
00:37:46.970 --> 00:37:49.010
We hold him indefinitely.

605
00:37:49.010 --> 00:37:51.680
Without so much
as the right to a phone call.

606
00:37:51.680 --> 00:37:54.600
Pretty sure the Constitution
says you can't do that.

607
00:37:54.600 --> 00:37:56.020
You're DEA.

608
00:37:56.020 --> 00:37:58.480
Grab some drugs from Evidence.
plant it in his car.

609
00:37:58.480 --> 00:38:00.770
say he was buying it from
some Central American dealer.

610
00:38:00.770 --> 00:38:02.400
then it becomes a narco-terrorism case.

611
00:38:02.400 --> 00:38:03.860
You can hold him as long as you want

612
00:38:03.860 --> 00:38:05.570
without formal charges
and no right to an attorney.

613
00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:09.320
- The law allows for that?
- It's kind of a gray area.

614
00:38:09.320 --> 00:38:12.540
A mouse's asshole is a gray area.
This is barely legal.

615
00:38:14.580 --> 00:38:16.580
But I don't think we have a choice.

616
00:38:16.580 --> 00:38:19.130
And while we got him.
we can question him. Good idea.

617
00:38:20.630 --> 00:38:22.250
Not just a pretty face.

618
00:38:23.800 --> 00:38:27.010
Okay. that takes care of our bodyguard.

619
00:38:27.010 --> 00:38:28.510
Who's playing our kidnapper?

620
00:38:31.850 --> 00:38:32.970
I'll do it.

621
00:38:32.970 --> 00:38:35.850
No. This one's
out of your comfort zone. precious.

622
00:38:35.850 --> 00:38:38.560
There's gonna be smashing cars.
flying glass.

623
00:38:38.560 --> 00:38:40.060
Villy. can you reel in someone
pulling a pension?

624
00:38:40.060 --> 00:38:41.060
No. No. Hell no.

625
00:38:41.060 --> 00:38:41.980
Excuse me?

626
00:38:43.360 --> 00:38:44.530
I'm the one who messed up the warrant.

627
00:38:44.530 --> 00:38:49.110
I'm the one who read the surveyor's map
wrong. set us up on private land.

628
00:38:49.110 --> 00:38:50.910
I'm gonna fix this.

629
00:38:53.040 --> 00:38:56.500
No brains. some balls.
Fine. you're our kidnapper.

630
00:38:56.500 --> 00:38:59.750
Okay. You'll make a move
for Richard. How do I stop you?

631
00:38:59.750 --> 00:39:02.420
He'll have a front row seat.
and fake fights look fake.

632
00:39:03.550 --> 00:39:04.840
We shoot him.

633
00:39:06.170 --> 00:39:07.800
Seriously?

634
00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:09.970
You're a fucking raccoon.

635
00:39:09.970 --> 00:39:12.260
<i>♪ Cut 'em down. tell 'em God Almighty's ♪</i>

636
00:39:12.260 --> 00:39:14.310
<i>♪ Gonna cut 'em down ♪</i>

637
00:39:14.310 --> 00:39:16.220
Are you sure this is safe?

638
00:39:16.220 --> 00:39:19.600
My buddy's kid uses 'em all the time
in these indie films he makes.

639
00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:22.860
- Buddy's kid.
- It's top quality stuff.

640
00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:24.730
Okay. don't move.

641
00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:29.320
Okay. point your finger
at the kid. say "bang."

642
00:39:30.450 --> 00:39:32.110
No.

643
00:39:32.120 --> 00:39:33.530
Christ's sakes. Bang.

644
00:39:33.530 --> 00:39:35.410
Is that great or what?

645
00:39:35.410 --> 00:39:37.660
I can hide nearby and set off the charges.

646
00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:41.420
Shit. Villy! Warn-warn me first!

647
00:39:41.420 --> 00:39:43.920
You're gonna give him a heart attack.
Hand it over.

648
00:39:45.130 --> 00:39:48.710
Jesus! Sh...
Come on. guys. it's not funny.

649
00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:50.510
Funny to me. Boys?

650
00:39:50.510 --> 00:39:51.840
Me. too.

651
00:39:51.840 --> 00:39:53.640
Kind of funny.

652
00:39:54.970 --> 00:39:56.100
<i>♪ Ugh...</i>

653
00:39:56.100 --> 00:39:59.480
After the fake grenade blast
and a gun fight.

654
00:39:59.480 --> 00:40:01.600
Richard won't come with me easily.

655
00:40:01.600 --> 00:40:03.650
-  You're making
an assumption--
-  No.

656
00:40:03.650 --> 00:40:05.940
In an investigation. assumptions kill.

657
00:40:05.940 --> 00:40:08.230
I'm making a reasonable prediction
that the college kid.

658
00:40:08.240 --> 00:40:10.990
who was just almost abducted
for the second time in his life.

659
00:40:10.990 --> 00:40:12.950
will be scared to death
and want the guy who saved him

660
00:40:12.950 --> 00:40:14.570
to take him to the cops.

661
00:40:14.570 --> 00:40:17.370
If he insists on that.
this is all a waste of time.

662
00:40:17.370 --> 00:40:19.080
He's not wrong. Villy.

663
00:40:20.870 --> 00:40:23.580
Refuse to do it. You'll be driving.
just take him home.

664
00:40:23.580 --> 00:40:26.590
That's suspicious. I'm trying
to infiltrate his dad's operation.

665
00:40:26.590 --> 00:40:29.090
We need as little suspicion as possible.

666
00:40:29.090 --> 00:40:30.260
<i>♪ Ugh...</i>

667
00:40:31.340 --> 00:40:32.840
So what do we do?

668
00:40:32.840 --> 00:40:35.470
We take the option of going to the police
completely off the table.

669
00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:37.810
How?

670
00:40:39.430 --> 00:40:41.310
I kill a cop.

671
00:40:44.860 --> 00:40:49.110
Time of day we're doing this.
streets should be mostly empty.

672
00:40:49.110 --> 00:40:51.440
We should give Eliot an Uzi.

673
00:40:51.440 --> 00:40:55.280
Rat-tat-tat of a machine gun
will scatter anyone nearby.

674
00:40:55.280 --> 00:40:57.070
Find me a panel van.

675
00:40:57.080 --> 00:41:00.200
I'll dive behind it for cover.
Eliot can really light it up.

676
00:41:00.200 --> 00:41:02.040
put on a convincing show.

677
00:41:04.170 --> 00:41:06.170
You know blanks alone won't sell this.

678
00:41:07.460 --> 00:41:09.840
Was wondering who was gonna say it first.

679
00:41:09.840 --> 00:41:11.880
I'll mix in some live ammo.

680
00:41:11.880 --> 00:41:14.680
I'll ditch the spent casings
before I get to Beck's house

681
00:41:14.680 --> 00:41:16.510
so they don't notice a difference.

682
00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:18.430
That lets me put a couple slugs
into the radiator

683
00:41:18.430 --> 00:41:20.260
of the kidnapper's ride.
and I can shoot out the tires

684
00:41:20.270 --> 00:41:22.100
before I kill Eliot and Villanueva
with blanks.

685
00:41:22.100 --> 00:41:23.560
Hmm.

686
00:41:27.810 --> 00:41:29.270
I like this plan.

687
00:41:30.360 --> 00:41:33.990
I don't like this plan.
Using live ammo is insane.

688
00:41:33.990 --> 00:41:36.240
What if you forget
how many shots you fired?

689
00:41:36.240 --> 00:41:37.780
There could be a real one
left in the chamber

690
00:41:37.780 --> 00:41:39.490
when you turn the gun on me or Eliot.

691
00:41:39.490 --> 00:41:40.780
You think about that. hotshot?

692
00:41:40.790 --> 00:41:42.490
Yeah. I did.

693
00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:45.410
- Did you get me the gun I asked for?
- Here.

694
00:41:45.420 --> 00:41:47.080
So what?

695
00:41:50.420 --> 00:41:52.130
You got a pocket knife?

696
00:42:03.480 --> 00:42:06.390
Now I always know
exactly where the blanks start.

697
00:42:11.690 --> 00:42:13.650
Best impound had to offer.

698
00:42:13.650 --> 00:42:15.570
Minivan will be
right by the dumpster.

699
00:42:15.570 --> 00:42:18.490
Coat hanger will be on top of the garbage.

700
00:42:19.570 --> 00:42:21.660
Door will be unlocked.
Just pretend to jimmy it.

701
00:42:23.200 --> 00:42:24.950
What's wrong?

702
00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:27.040
I don't know how to hot-wire a car.

703
00:42:27.040 --> 00:42:29.830
We'll loosen the shroud on
the steering column. pre-strip the wires.

704
00:42:29.830 --> 00:42:31.960
You touch them together.
you're an instant bad guy.

705
00:42:31.960 --> 00:42:34.840
I've also been thinking
about the street layout.

706
00:42:34.840 --> 00:42:37.170
Your best vantage point.
before everything jumps off.

707
00:42:37.180 --> 00:42:39.470
is from inside the record shop.

708
00:42:39.470 --> 00:42:41.140
But you'll need a reason
to hang out in there.

709
00:42:41.140 --> 00:42:42.390
And?

710
00:42:42.390 --> 00:42:44.100
And I got you covered.

711
00:42:52.020 --> 00:42:53.690
What am I supposed to do with these?

712
00:42:53.690 --> 00:42:55.190
Record store buys old vinyl.

713
00:42:55.190 --> 00:42:57.280
Just pretend you want
to sell my collection.

714
00:43:00.280 --> 00:43:01.320
Won't work.

715
00:43:01.320 --> 00:43:02.700
Why not?

716
00:43:02.700 --> 00:43:05.660
'Cause no one'll believe anyone thinks
they can get a nickel for this crap.

717
00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:07.500
Fuck you.

718
00:43:13.090 --> 00:43:15.550
<i>Ethel Merman Disco Album?</i>

719
00:43:23.720 --> 00:43:25.810
No duck tonight?

720
00:43:25.810 --> 00:43:28.270
Probably doesn't want to be
a part of this plan.

721
00:43:33.230 --> 00:43:34.940
Don't think we can pull it off?

722
00:43:34.940 --> 00:43:38.030
If we can set off the bullet hits
at exactly the right time.

723
00:43:38.030 --> 00:43:40.780
and if no one actually gets shot.

724
00:43:40.780 --> 00:43:44.200
and if you can keep that bodyguard
pinned down long enough.

725
00:43:44.200 --> 00:43:45.830
I only see two potential problems.

726
00:43:45.830 --> 00:43:48.700
- Okay. hit me.
- Cops.

727
00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:51.870
Shootout will be over pretty fast. but
they'll definitely show up after the fact.

728
00:43:51.880 --> 00:43:54.670
And I'll be there to tell them
it's a drug deal gone south.

729
00:43:54.670 --> 00:43:57.590
it's an active DEA investigation.
and our jurisdiction.

730
00:43:57.590 --> 00:43:58.840
What about campus security?

731
00:43:58.840 --> 00:44:00.840
Rent-a-cops like to play hero sometimes.

732
00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:03.510
Small department with no regular patrol.

733
00:44:03.510 --> 00:44:05.470
I mean. if they happen to cross your path.

734
00:44:05.470 --> 00:44:07.350
you'll have to dispose of them.

735
00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:11.350
Without causing injury.

736
00:44:15.400 --> 00:44:16.730
What's the second problem?

737
00:44:16.730 --> 00:44:19.030
Communication.

738
00:44:19.030 --> 00:44:20.360
How do we stay in touch?

739
00:44:22.860 --> 00:44:26.660
I think I got the size right.

740
00:44:26.660 --> 00:44:29.660
You know what they say about a man
with big feet. don't you?

741
00:44:29.660 --> 00:44:33.960
More room in his boot heel
to hide a secret phone.

742
00:44:35.590 --> 00:44:37.880
Government issue. satellite-linked.

743
00:44:37.880 --> 00:44:39.880
pretty much untraceable.

744
00:44:39.880 --> 00:44:41.720
14-day battery life.

745
00:44:41.720 --> 00:44:45.510
If you need me.
I am just a phone call away.

746
00:44:52.730 --> 00:44:55.020
<i>You're in?
So he hired you?</i>

747
00:44:55.020 --> 00:44:57.980
Yeah. Interesting job interview.

748
00:44:57.980 --> 00:45:00.030
Made me play Russian roulette.

749
00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:02.320
Probably thought
it was more theatrical that way.

750
00:45:02.320 --> 00:45:04.450
<i>Fuck. You did it?</i>

751
00:45:04.450 --> 00:45:05.990
I used my own gun.

752
00:45:05.990 --> 00:45:07.910
I had a chamber marked. remember?

753
00:45:07.910 --> 00:45:10.080
I put the bullet in that one so.
even with the cylinder closed.

754
00:45:10.080 --> 00:45:11.450
I always knew where it was.

755
00:45:11.450 --> 00:45:13.290
What if the one with the bullet
had come up?

756
00:45:13.290 --> 00:45:16.290
<i>I'd have shot the armed guy behind me
and tried to fight my way out.</i>

757
00:45:17.880 --> 00:45:19.710
- Any leads on Quinn?
<i>- Not yet.</i>

758
00:45:19.710 --> 00:45:21.340
How's the bodyguard?

759
00:45:21.340 --> 00:45:23.590
He's in the adjoining room.

760
00:45:25.180 --> 00:45:27.680
We patched him up. took a few runs at him.

761
00:45:27.680 --> 00:45:29.260
but he's not saying shit.

762
00:45:29.260 --> 00:45:31.390
<i>Claims he spends most of his time
with Richard</i>

763
00:45:31.390 --> 00:45:34.020
<i>- and has no idea what we're talking about.</i>
- You believe him?

764
00:45:34.020 --> 00:45:35.980
I don't know.

765
00:45:35.980 --> 00:45:38.110
Well. I might have a lead on the girl.

766
00:45:38.110 --> 00:45:40.980
Beck's head of security
carried a plate of food outside.

767
00:45:40.980 --> 00:45:42.480
Could've been taking it
to the carriage house

768
00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:44.650
where I think there's a hidden cellar.

769
00:45:44.650 --> 00:45:46.780
I'll wait till everyone's asleep.

770
00:45:46.780 --> 00:45:48.370
At 3:00 a.m.. I'll check it out.

771
00:45:48.370 --> 00:45:50.330
Keep me posted.

772
00:49:15.370 --> 00:49:17.370
-  <i>Reacher.</i>
- I'm in the cellar.

773
00:49:17.370 --> 00:49:19.240
<i>Is Teresa there?</i>

774
00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:25.080
No.

775
00:49:26.500 --> 00:49:28.130
